  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Capacities and Frameworks to Collect Data and Evidence on Migration, the Environment and Climate Change in Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed intervention aims to build the foundation for evidence-based policymaking on environmental migration in Mexico by building innovative tools and methodologies to collect data and information on the nexus between human mobility and disasters, the adverse effects of climate change and environmental degradation. This will be accomplished by equipping the Government of Mexico &#x2013; in particular, the National Institute of Statistics and Geography (INEGI), the Migration Policy, Registry, and Identity of Persons Unit (UPMRIP) in the Secretariat of the Interior (SEGOB), INECC, SEMARNAT, and municipal and state planning authorities with a number of innovative, tested methodological and analytical tools (including, among other resources, guides, toolkits, methodological notes, and a diagnostic) to measure dynamics of environmental migration.</narrative>
  </description>
